      "title": "Missing Australian hiker Jordan Yap last seen on remote trail found dead in Peru",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/11/missing-australian-hiker-jordan-yap-last-seen-on-remote-trail-found-dead-in-peru",
      "description": "<p>Family and friends say Melbourne man should be remembered for ‘immense joy he brought to so many people’s lives’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>An Australian trekker who was last seen on a remote South American hiking trail has been found dead, his family have said.</p><p>Jordan Yap, 30, last made contact with friends and family on 14 September ahead of a planned 10-day solo trek along Peru’s Huayhuash mountain range, 400km north-east of Lima.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/11/missing-australian-hiker-jordan-yap-last-seen-on-remote-trail-found-dead-in-peru\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-11T07:45:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "Australia has never driven migration into reverse by design. Would slamming the brakes on be calamitous?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/12/australia-has-never-driven-migration-into-reverse-by-design-would-slamming-the-brakes-on-be-calamitous",
      "description": "<p>Australia does have a migration challenge – but it’s not what One Nation and the Coalition think it is</p><ul><li><p><strong>Get our </strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\"><strong>new political email</strong></a><strong>, </strong><a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\"><strong>free app</strong></a><strong> or </strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\"><strong>daily news podcast</strong></a></p></li></ul><p>Australia is flirting with the idea of something it has never done: deliberately driving <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/08/net-overseas-migration-how-do-policies-compare-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">net overseas migration into reverse</a>.</p><p>In the history of our immigrant nation, extended periods of more people leaving our shores than arriving have only happened during convulsive moments: economic collapses, wars, and pandemics.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/12/australia-has-never-driven-migration-into-reverse-by-design-would-slamming-the-brakes-on-be-calamitous\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-11T14:00:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Greens gear up for fight with Labor as Sarah Hanson-Young pushes to strengthen laws to rein in big tech",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/12/greens-sarah-hanson-young-big-tech-digital-duty-of-care-labor",
      "description": "<p>Minor party plans to drive a tough bargain in exchange for support for digital duty of care legislation</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Greens will push Labor to dramatically toughen new laws designed to rein in big tech, calling for individuals to have the right to take platforms to court and win financial compensation.</p><p>As Labor prepares to introduce its planned <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/08/australia-social-media-algorithm-switch-off-opt-out-digital-duty-of-care\">digital duty of care laws</a> into parliament this week, the Greens say they will drive a tough bargain in exchange for support, including pushing for fines by the eSafety commissioner to be levied as a percentage of corporations’ global revenue rather than set amounts.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/12/greens-sarah-hanson-young-big-tech-digital-duty-of-care-labor\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-11T14:00:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "A Trump impersonator and opera singers: CPAC was a spectacle, but the right still can’t agree how to take down Labor",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/11/a-trump-impersonator-and-opera-singers-cpac-was-a-spectacle-but-the-right-still-cant-agree-how-to-take-down-labor-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Preferences proved the sticking point at the conference as conservatives face the prospect of a third successive election defeat</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Many mainstream Australians would feel as if they’d been dropped in a foreign country at the Conservative Political Action Conference, lost amid oblique references to transgender swimmers, blue hair, women’s bathrooms, jokes about <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2025/apr/24/did-albanese-fall-off-a-stage-or-not-and-why-do-people-keep-talking-about-it\">falling off stages</a> and Matt Canavan in hi-vis and <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/watch/?v=1100308805718182\">speed dealer sunnies</a>.</p><p>It’s an interesting spectacle. At this year’s conference in Brisbane, rightwing campaigner Monica Smit was deep in conversation with a Donald Trump impersonator, opera singers belted out the national anthem (the first verse, twice, for unknown reasons), senator Jacinta Nampijinpa Price and her folk singer husband sang <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DeTPyIJgvyQ/?hl=en\">the anthem again</a>, and Karl Stefanovic jokingly thanking CPAC for “rudely interrupting my unemployment”.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/11/a-trump-impersonator-and-opera-singers-cpac-was-a-spectacle-but-the-right-still-cant-agree-how-to-take-down-labor-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-11T06:47:17"
    },
